## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-DC data residency controls, real-time policy updates, and secure audit logging in a docker-dca setup.

## Key Concepts
- Data residency and cross-DC egress policies
- WASM-based per-tenant policy engine (Wasmtime)
- Vault-driven tenant configs and SPIFFE SVID rotation
- SIEM-based auditing and reproducible bootstrap

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluation sketch
function evaluate(event, tenant) {
  if (event.destDC === 'DC-B' && !tenant.optIn) return 'block';
  redact(event.payload, tenant.schema);
  return 'allow';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify policy correctness across DC failover?
- How would you handle policy module hot-reload and versioning?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical secret lifecycle management in Docker Swarm, integrating Vault for automated rotation with zero-downtime upgrades and proper secret versioning.

## Key Concepts
- Swarm secrets versioning and dynamic reattachment
- Vault-based rotation triggers and secret provisioning
- Rolling updates with start-first strategy to avoid downtime
- Health checks to confirm new secrets are loaded before removing old ones
- Atomic secret updates using add-then-remove pattern

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-automation: rotate Vault-derived Swarm secrets
async function rotateSecrets(serviceName, vaultPath) {
  // Fetch new credentials from Vault
  const newCreds = await vault.read(vaultPath);

  // Create new Swarm secrets
  const newSecrets = await createSwarmSecrets(newCreds);

  // Update service with new secrets
  await updateService(serviceName, newSecrets);

  // Verify health before cleanup
  await verifyServiceHealth(serviceName);

  // Remove old secrets
  await cleanupOldSecrets(serviceName);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant QoS with dynamic config in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Traefik RateLimit middleware, Redis store, per-tenant quotas, Docker Config
- TLS termination, hot-reload without restart, cross-DC coordination
- Request tagging with X-Tenant and validation of isolation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo middleware sketch: extract tenant and enforce quota from Redis
async function enforceTenantRate(req, res, next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const quota = await redisGetQuota(tenant);
  if (quota.allow(req)) return next();
  res.status(429).send('Too Many Requests');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit cross-DC quota drift and recover from Redis replication lag?
- How would you test hot-reload behavior under config churn?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design tenant-aware data residency and policy enforcement in docker-dca, including edge TLS termination, overlay data paths, and canary safety net.

## Key Concepts
- docker-dca multi-DC deployment
- SPIFFE/SVID rotation with Vault
- data residency via overlay networks/volumes
- per-tenant policy with OPA
- canary rollout and rollback criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code illustrating policy check
const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
if (allowedTenants[tenant]?.includes(req.path)) {
  next();
} else {
  res.status(403).send('forbidden');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor cross-tenant data access to ensure residency is respected?
- How would you test the canary rollback under sudden quota breach?
